---
/**
 * The wood grain behind a dark section.
 *
 * Deliberately an <img> rather than a CSS background: a background-image is
 * discovered during CSS parse and fetched immediately, which put this file on
 * the wire at 92ms competing with the fonts, even though the section it
 * belongs to is thousands of pixels down the page. As an <img> it lazy-loads
 * like everything else.
 *
 * Purely decorative, so it carries an empty alt and is hidden from assistive
 * technology.
 */
---

<div class="grain" aria-hidden="true">
  <img
    src="/images/texture/dark-grain.webp"
    alt=""
    width="1400"
    height="950"
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async"
  />
</div>
